1,2 $ Cystidia absent
1,3 $ Cystidia present
1,0$
1,0$ source :/// Novelties in the Corticiales: Vuilleminia nilsii sp. nov. and Dendrominia gen. nov. (Basidiomycota) /// Masoomeh Ghobad-Nejhad • Bernard Duhem- Mycological Progress_13-1_2014 
2,0 $ Spores allantoid, (15-)16.5-22.6(-24)x(4.2-)5.3- 7.3(-8) µm, Qmean=3.5; mature basidia 10-12.5 µm wide $ V. comedens
2,0 $ Spores broadly ellipsoid-ovoid to fusoid, (19.5-)22- 28(-32)x (9-)11-13.5(-16) µm, Qmean=2; mature basidia 15-17.5 µm wide µm megalospora
3,0 $ Cystidia enclosed, scarcely differentiated, with apical appendix, spores (11.8-)12-15.5(-16.2)x3-4.6(-5.2) µm $ V. erastii
3,4 $ Cystidia projecting above hymenium, well differentiated, apex obtuse, tapering, or capitate, spore sizes different
4,5 $ Cystidia with tapering to apex, or capitate
4,6 $ . Cystidia with obtuse apex
5,0 $ Fruiting body decorticating; cystidia tapering; spores (9.5-)13-18.3(-20)x(3.3-)3.8-6.2(-7.1) µm, lacking or with very few oil-like droplets $ V. cystidiata
5,0 $ Fruiting body decorticating or on bark; cystidia capitate; spores (12-)13-16.5 (-17.5)x(4.1-)5-6.5(-7.1) µm, usually with prominent oil-like droplets $ V. macrospora
6,0 $ Spores (10.5-)12.5-17(-18)x(3.2-)3.5-5(-5.4) µm, without granular contents; basidia 50-72x4-7 µm, arranged in a very dense and compact hymenium $ V. pseudocystidiata
6,7 $ Spores larger, up to 5-8 µm wide, with granular contents; basidia larger, not in a dense hymenium
7,0 $ Spores (15.5-)16.5-22(-24.5)x5-7(-8) µm ; hyphae smooth; dendrohyphidia abundant; often on Corylus  and many others broad-leaved trees but not recorded on Quercus $ V. coryli
7,0 $ Spores smaller, (14.5-)15-17.5(-18)x5-6(-6.2) µm ; hyphae heavily crystallized; dendrohyphidia scarce; on Quercus pubescens and Q. ilex $ V. nilsii

